83828.sol:
Key Idea : Phase difference =$\frac{2 \pi}{\lambda}$ \times $\text{ path difference }$
Path difference between two points,
$\Delta x=15-10=5 \mathrm{~m}
Time period, $T=0.05 $\mathrm{~s}$\Rightarrow$ frequency $v=$\frac{1}{T}=\frac{1}{0.05}=$20 $\mathrm{~Hz}$
Velocity, $y=300 \mathrm{~m} / \mathrm{s}\therefore$ Wavelength, $\lambda=\frac{v}{v}=\frac{300}{20}=15 \mathrm{~m}
Hence, phase difference
$\begin{aligned}
\Delta \phi & =$\frac{2 \pi}{\lambda}$ \times \Delta x \\
& =$\frac{2 \pi}{15}$ \times 5=$\frac{2 \pi}{3}$
\end{aligned}

